exports[`create output > help 1`] = `
{
  "argv": [
    "--help",
  ],
  "exit": 0,
  "exitCode": undefined,
  "files": {},
  "stderr": "",
  "stdout": "Usage: npm create @indx-workspace <dir> -- [options]

Writes a project that \`aw dev\` runs. Each setup question can be answered by a flag; the
rest are asked on a terminal, and take their default with no terminal or with --yes.

Options:
  --yes       take the default for every question not answered by a flag, ask nothing,
              install the dependencies, and do not start the dev server
  --answers <file>   setup answers in a YAML or JSON file, keyed by question id; flags win
  --install / --no-install   install the dependencies after writing (asked on a terminal)
  --start / --no-start       run \`dev\` after installing (asked on a terminal); it stays in
                             the foreground until Ctrl-C and create exits with its code
  --template <portal | chat | wiki | crm | desk>
              also write an app (not with --cloud): portal adds a Next.js app with dashboard,
              chat, files and runs pages; chat, wiki, crm and desk are presets over it with
              the recipe pages, the wiki its spaces and pages, the desk its dashboard; a
              preset takes --theme blank unless --theme is given; the README lists the
              commands that build the app on
  --help      print this text

With no terminal, or with CI set, nothing is asked: flags, --answers and defaults are used.

Setup flags:
  --theme <support | copilot | knowledge | automation | review | blank>
      Which theme should setup start from? (default: support)
  --sandbox <auto | local>
      Where should agents run their tools? (default: auto)
  --provider <anthropic | anthropic-compatible | openai | azure-openai | openai-compatible>
      Who serves the agent's model? (default: anthropic)
  --model-base-url <an http(s) URL without a credential, up to 2048 characters>
      Where is the model provider's endpoint? (required when --provider is anthropic-compatible or openai-compatible or azure-openai; no default)
  --agent <lower-case letters, digits and hyphens, 1-64 characters, no hyphen at either end>
      What is your first agent called? (default: assistant)
  --engine <claude-agent-sdk | openai-agents | pi | mastra>
      Which agent engine should it use? (default: claude-agent-sdk)
  --tools <openapi | postgres | none; comma-separated>
      Which internal tools should the agent call? (default: none)
  --openapi <a project-relative path to a .json, .yaml or .yml file, or an https URL without a credential, up to 2048 characters>
      Where is the OpenAPI document? (default: openapi.json)
  --permissions <readFiles | writeFiles | runCommands | unrestrictedNetwork; comma-separated>
      Which permissions should the agent have? (default: )
  --title <1-60 characters, no control or invisible characters, no space at either end>
      What title should the chat widget show? (default: Assistant)
  --color <a hex colour, # followed by six hex digits>
      What is your brand colour? (default: #2f5fd0)
  --platform <claude-managed-agents | copilot-studio | m365-declarative-agent | microsoft-foundry | gemini-enterprise | aws-agentcore | none; comma-separated>
      Which agent platforms should this agent also be published to? (default: none)
  --features <chat | projects | files | skills | connectors | runs | sharing | surfaces | triggers | evaluations | builder; comma-separated>
      Which features should this deployment include? (default: chat,projects,files,skills,connectors,runs,sharing,surfaces,triggers,evaluations,builder)

Deployment project (v1):
  --cloud <aws | gcp | azure | local | vercel | cloudflare>
  --validate  with --cloud, probe the generated stores
  --yes       with --cloud local, take the default of every question below
  --port <n>  with --cloud local, publish the web service on this host port (default 3000)
  --database <text>, --storage <text>, --runtime <text>, --auth <text>
              with --cloud local, answer the question of that name (defaults: PostgreSQL 18 (container); local filesystem (Docker volume); docker; local administrator)
",
}
`;

